Amendment: divider between the husbok and "How Home Base works" sections
(Phase 4, home_page_rebuild_20260906)

REQUESTED
Owner: 'Add a divider between A tradition worth keeping and How Home Base works.'

WHAT CHANGED
  M components/landing/landing-how.tsx  border-t border-landing-hairline on the section
  M spec.md                             section table note and FR5

WHY IT WAS MISSING
Fallout from removing the "Why it matters" band. In the prototype that dark slab sat
between these two sections and did the dividing. Both neighbours sit on paper, so cutting
the slab left them running together with nothing but padding between them. This is the
kind of gap that only shows up once the composition is seen whole, which is why it
surfaced at review rather than while the section was being built.

WHY A FULL-BLEED HAIRLINE
It matches the footer's existing border-t treatment, so the page has one vocabulary for
"a boundary between bands" rather than two. A container-inset rule would have competed
with the inset rules already inside this section — the one above the four columns, and
the short brass rule under the husbok heading.

VERIFICATION PERFORMED
  npm run build -> exit 0, Compiled successfully in 10.6s, 39/39 static pages.
  node scripts/verify-landing-contrast.mjs -> ALL PASS. The hairline token was already
    covered: 1.62:1 on paper in light, 1.55:1 in dark, against a 1.4:1 floor.
  Computed style on the section, light theme:
    border-top: 1px solid lab(79.978 0.802934 -2.90442)  -- the hairline token
  Visual, both themes, against the production build on :3100: the rule reads as a quiet
    boundary in light and in dark, and does not compete with the column rule below it.
